    "b-sks-lifecycle-resolution-p": {
      "id": "b-sks-lifecycle-resolution-p",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "An evidence row is a fact-owned citation — a typed "
        },
        {
          "insert": "locator",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " into one of the knowledge sources, a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "why",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " saying how the pointed-at record supports the claim, and — for "
        },
        {
          "insert": "code",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " only — a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "digest",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " of the span text. No content is snapshotted on the row; display resolves the locator into the source at read time. A row claims nothing itself, and citing a record does not mean it states the claim: the connection from observation to claim is the owning fact's "
        },
        {
          "insert": "rationale",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". The resolver checks every evidence row when the fact is written — the locator must match its "
        },
        {
          "insert": "kind",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "'s closed grammar and resolve to a source row, and a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "code",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " row's digest must match the span — and the drift flagger re-resolves "
        },
        {
          "insert": "code://",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " locators later; the other sources are immutable and cannot drift."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
